              "type": "Type"
            }
          ],
          "content": "This Cambay \u2013 a housecoat and matching waistcoat \u2013 was made in the Netherlands using cotton cloth from India. The robe\u2019s fabric has a blue zigzag pattern derived from European woven silks of the 1720s. European silk with Asian motifs was called \u2018bizarre\u2019, and these patterns, in turn, were used in the production of cotton chintz in India."
        },
        {
          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "classified_as": [
            {
